      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Charlottetown"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Charlottetown Conference that sparked Canada’s unification met inside Province House, now part of the Confederation Centre of the Arts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Charlottetown"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Charlottetown sits on a harbour created where the Hillsborough, North River, and East River meet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlottetown"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Fort Amherst, built by British forces near the abandoned Port La Joye settlement, guards the harbour entrance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
